  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final text sets an 8% permanent S2 market-entry cap with no public publication of per-model rates, but gives buyers per-model results, which keeps the Hearth 10 (6.2%) on sale. S5 makes recall mandatory only above 10 per 100,000, leaving the Ember 8 (9.9) outside mandatory recall, with an open-ended corrective-action band between 8 and 10. S1 is the strongest section, with 24-hour reporting and customer notice for all thermal incidents, and S3 and S4 sit at the edges of their acceptable ranges (24-month new-unit shut-off; 36-month suppression)."
